config RPMSG_ECHO_MU_KICK_ID
	int "MU register used to kick the host"
	default -1
	help
	  MU data register the host listens on: with Linux imx_rproc, the
	  index of its "rx" mbox channel (mboxes = <&mu 1 N>). On a kick,
	  imx_rproc processes every vring, so all kicks go to that register.
	  -1 kicks on the register numbered like the vring, as Zephyr's
	  openamp_rsc_table sample does.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
